
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F : Points
CB = CA [00]
A,D,C are collinear [01]
CD = CE [02]
C,E,B are collinear [03]
A,F,E are collinear [04]
D,F,B are collinear [05]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. CB = CA [00] & CD = CE [02] ⇒  CB:CA = CD:CE [06]
002. CB = CA [00] & CD = CE [02] ⇒  CB:CA = CE:CD [07]
003. C,E,B are collinear [03] & C,D,A are collinear [01] ⇒  ∠BCA = ∠ECD [08]
004. CB:CA = CD:CE [06] & ∠BCA = ∠ECD [08] (Similar Triangles)⇒  CD:CB = DE:AB [09]
005. CB:CA = CE:CD [07] & ∠BCA = ∠ECD [08] (Similar Triangles)⇒  ∠CBA = ∠CED [10]
006. ∠CBA = ∠CED [10] & C,E,B are collinear [03] ⇒  AB ∥ DE [11]
007. AB ∥ DE [11] & A,F,E are collinear [04] & D,F,B are collinear [05] ⇒  FE:AF = DE:AB [12]
008. AB ∥ DE [11] & A,F,E are collinear [04] & D,F,B are collinear [05] ⇒  FE:AF = DF:FB [13]
009. CD:CB = DE:AB [09] & FE:AF = DE:AB [12] & FE:AF = DF:FB [13] ⇒  FD:FB = CD:CB [14]
010. FD:FB = CD:CB [14] & D,F,B are collinear [05] ⇒  ∠DCF = ∠FCB [15]
011. ∠DCF = ∠FCB [15] & A,D,C are collinear [01] ⇒  ∠ACF = ∠FCB
==========================
